{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/844117-how-big-is-big","id":844117,"title":"How Big is Big?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-08T13:10:26-08:00","id":844117,"title":"How Big is Big?","content":"This is a question that first came up among my gaming group and other friends when talking about a new Gurahl (were-bear) character but then dissolved into all sorts of different groups. But basically, we could not come to a consensus over what constitutes a &quot;big character.&quot; Everyone seemed to agree that a 6'4 in height and muscular character was large but everything after that was all over the place. For some of the more diminutive debaters anything over 6'1 and with a decent build was considered big while some of the taller combatants stuck to only that 6'4 or so and above range (something like 6'2 was considered clearly above average but not big enough to justify a were-bear, a big Viking Scion of Thor, any other large template you can think of). So I thought would bring the question to here, for you all when playing &quot;large&quot; characters, what sort of size range do you consider that to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T00:18:13-08:00","id":844372,"title":"","content":"Very relative question.<br /> <br /> But over 7 feet in height.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T08:29:38-08:00","id":844525,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine is 6' 10&quot; and boy is he big. But Huge Size is seven feet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:59:30-08:00","id":844652,"title":"","content":"As a person that reached 6' in height by the age of 12, I've always considered anyone at least roughly my size (now only 6' 3&quot;) as being &quot;big&quot;<br /> <br /> If we are talking about where I draw the line for what qualifies as &quot;big&quot; in the sense of their being mechanical adjustments that apply to the game, then I go with &quot;however big a person would have to be to need to duck and/or angle-in to walk through through my front door&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T16:00:19-08:00","id":844777,"title":"","content":"Did you see the 2nd Peter Jackson Hobbit movie? Did you see Bjorn and how he towered even over Gandalf, who's taller than even some of the other humans? That's the kind of guy they had in mind when writing that merit and the Gurahl in general.<br /> <br /> If a hobbit can run between your legs without ducking, you have the Huge Size Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:46:03-08:00","id":845455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/844117-how-big-is-big?p=844777#post844777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a hobbit can run between your legs without ducking, you have the Huge Size Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno man, even if I was Bjorn's height and a hobbit went to go between my legs and didn't look like they were going to duck, I'd jump a little (because once, long ago when my eldest nephew was still in diapers, I took a full toddler-sprint-powered headbutt to danglies - and I am thus quite certain I never want a repeat of the incident).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:43:42-08:00","id":845684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/844117-how-big-is-big?p=845455#post845455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno man, even if I was Bjorn's height and a hobbit went to go between my legs and didn't look like they were going to duck, I'd jump a little (because once, long ago when my eldest nephew was still in diapers, I took a full toddler-sprint-powered headbutt to danglies - and I am thus quite certain I never want a repeat of the incident).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, been there, done that. 2 Baby Bears at home. I jump when they just get close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:38:09-08:00","id":845780,"title":"","content":"The question was more for just subjective ideas of what is &quot;big,&quot; not so much stat adjustments coming in to play. I think we can all agree that 7 ft 400 lbs or whatever it is for the Merit is big :P <br /> The Gurahl player that sort of sparked this whole thing in our group, for example, saw his character at around 6'2 and a muscular 225-230. That's like NFL linebacker size but not NFL lineman. Some felt for a Gurahl or any sort of template that is larger, that just wasn't big enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T16:26:06-08:00","id":845867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/844117-how-big-is-big?p=845455#post845455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno man, even if I was Bjorn's height and a hobbit went to go between my legs and didn't look like they were going to duck, I'd jump a little (because once, long ago when my eldest nephew was still in diapers, I took a full toddler-sprint-powered headbutt to danglies - and I am thus quite certain I never want a repeat of the incident).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> LMFAO, I almost peed myself, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T15:20:18-08:00","id":846296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merinoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/844117-how-big-is-big?p=845780#post845780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gurahl player that sort of sparked this whole thing in our group, for example, saw his character at around 6'2 and a muscular 225-230. That's like NFL linebacker size but not NFL lineman. Some felt for a Gurahl or any sort of template that is larger, that just wasn't big enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's not &quot;big enough&quot; for a Gurahl, that implies that something like a 5' 8&quot; and fairly muscular person isn't &quot;big enough&quot; for a werewolf, or that a 6' 0&quot; and incredibly lanky person is &quot;too big&quot; for a corvus (corvid? I forget the term for were-ravens... all these terms come from my least-read WoD game line).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}